meta {
  name: Get Profile
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/client/me
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

docs {
  # Get Client Profile

  The account's profile plus **where it stands as a master** — the app decides
  from this single response whether to show "become a master", the review
  status, or the role switch. No second request needed.

  **Response 200:**
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Merdan Annagurdow",
      "phone": "+99361111222",
      "city_id": 1,
      "city": { "id": 1, "name": "Ашхабад" },
      "master_status": "approved",
      "master_id": 7,
      "has_master_access": true,
      "created_at": "2026-08-15 10:00:00"
    }
  }
  ```

  | Field               | Values                                        |
  |---------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
  | `master_status`     | `null` / `pending` / `approved` / `rejected`  |
  | `master_id`         | master profile id, `null` when never applied  |
  | `has_master_access` | approved **and** active **and** subscribed     |

  Poll this (or `05_become_master` → Get Application) to notice the
  administrator's verdict while the applicant waits.
}
